From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: back micro-cuts from #1586, the draw side (EDEN_UP_BACKX_DRAW=1, off unless set)

Upstream: zortos293/Lichii 5e428570d2 (PR #1586, Zortos (zortos293) with capy-ai), micro-cuts 2-5:
the vertex input cache from jpkto/Lichii e7581fa9f6, the fast-draw clock from DahBard/Lichii
b95617b80f, uniform streaks from skolvolt/Lichii 9267908a3d, the break counter from lucastaonline's
865afaa4f3 (#1161).

EDEN_UP_BACKX_DRAW=1 (exact "1"):
- UpdateVertexInput keeps built dynamic vertex input states in a 256-entry direct-mapped cache
  (new video_core/vertex_input_cache.h) keyed by every register the build reads (attribute format
  words, stream strides, divisors, instancing, repacked bindings, device limits) and records them
  by shared reference. With EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW_VERIFY a hit is also built fresh and compared (an
  error line, and the fresh one is recorded, on a difference). Our build keeps its repacked offset
  (+3) and stride (72), both covered by the repacked bits of the key.
- PrepareDraw reads the fast-draw prepare clock (two fenced time stamps a draw) only when
  ReportFastDraws logs it (EDEN_NX2_GPU_PROFILE or EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW_VERIFY).
- BindSmallUniformReusing: after 8 binds in a row whose bytes differ from the slot's last, the
  slot's next 64 binds read guest memory straight into its bytes and stream them, without the
  scratch read and memcmp; a bind of the same bytes ends a streak. The slot's ref, tick, range and
  bytes stay the bind's own (EDEN_UP_L949_UBO_KEEP and its verify unchanged); EDEN_UP_UBO_SHARE
  is tried first as before.
- Nx2FastDraw::Break on the drawing thread skips the locked add once one of its breaks moved the
  serial since its last Serial() read (every read re-arms); other threads always add. g_serial
  moves to its own cache line (always; layout only).
The count line is 1004's (HW_GPU, every 10 s): "draw: vertex input builds N cache hits N, clock
skips N, uniform streaks N direct binds N, break adds skipped N". Unset: as before.
Not taken: upstream's #1519 vertex-input verify plumbing (T182 ports #1519 separately; a merge
will meet in UpdateVertexInput). No translation id input: KEEPS THE STORE.

